#DESCRIPTION
3D Standalone Martian Magnetosphere regression test of the full boundary setup:
Semi-Implicit Full PIC on a coarse 24 x 32 x 32 grid (dx = 0.25 R_M), 10 s.
Same deck as run_mars/final_coarse (stable to 200 s), shortened to 10 s and
2 x 2 x 2 particles per cell.
Physics & Features:
- c = uNormSI = 3000 km/s (10x the solar wind).
- Absorbing, conducting body at 3590 km (200 km altitude, rhybrid particle obstacle),
  made floating (FLOATINGBODY): the net electron charge it absorbs is re-emitted.
- Ionospheric emission shell at 3790 km (IONOSPHEREEMISSION, rhybrid): O2+ 2e25/s,
  O+ 1.4e25/s, 20000 K; the photochemical boundary is at the shell.
- Mixed exosphere: hot H (Chamberlain) and hot O coronae (rhybrid), cold O and CO2.
- 13-reaction photochemistry, EUV optical depth, Parker-spiral IMF.
- Inflow at +x (300 km/s); open (outflowthermal) faces elsewhere.

